# Why we chose X over Y

> **Directive (assistant):** When the user makes a durable decision — picking one
> tool, stack, or approach over the alternatives — capture the *reasoning* in a
> `knowledge/why-we-chose-<thing>.md` file. Record the decision, the context that
> forced it, the options considered with their main trade-offs, the one or two
> factors that actually decided it (be honest about the trade-off accepted), and
> the condition under which it should be revisited. Capturing the *why* stops a
> future session from re-litigating a settled choice or quietly undoing it.

This is the model for the understanding layer — long-form reasoning, not a fact or
a rule. It is read on demand via `rekol search`, not injected every session, so it
can hold the longer-form story. Keep each rationale to roughly one screen. Until
you have a real decision to record, leave the body empty below this directive.
